  "description": "Vertical machining center. The failure content is grounded in what actually breaks these machines: lubrication is the single most critical maintenance task, contaminated coolant and poor lubrication are the leading causes of premature bearing and ballscrew failure, and a majority of spindle shutdowns trace to lubrication that was missed or not recorded. A spindle rebuild is $5k-$50k and 1-4 weeks of downtime.",

